    "notes": "1. 'Total revenues and other income' is mapped to 'total_revenue' and is composed of the three listed line items. 2. 'Total operating cost' is constructed for the oil & gas industry to include all operating expenses before interest and income taxes. This includes: cost of goods sold ('Crude oil and product purchases'), operating expenses ('Production and manufacturing', 'Selling, general and administrative', 'Depreciation and depletion', 'Exploration'), and other operating charges ('Non-service pension/postretirement expense', 'Other taxes and duties'). 'Other taxes and duties' are considered operating costs as they are primarily production, property, and excise taxes. 3. 'Net income' is mapped to the line attributable to the parent company. 4. 'Taxes' is mapped to 'Income tax expense'. 5. 'Interest expense' is mapped directly. 6. Supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns (e.g., components of 'Other income', 'Depreciation and depletion', 'Other taxes and duties', 'Income tax expense') but the primary statement provides the aggregated values used here. 7. Numbers in parentheses in the source (e.g., (609)) are treated as negative values in the supplementary context but are not directly used in the aggregated fields extracted from the primary statement.",
